      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(canvas): surface eval errors instead of silently swallowing them",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nWhen `canvas.eval` returns a non-string result or error from the node (e.g. `{ payload: { error: \"SyntaxError: Unexpected token\" } }`), the old code returned `jsonResult({ ok: true })` — a generic success signal. The agent sees success even when the JavaScript evaluation failed.\n\n## Root Cause\n\nThe `raw` cast at `tool.ts:160-162` only recognized `{ payload?: { result?: string } }`. When `result` was absent or non-string (number, null, undefined), control fell through to `return jsonResult({ ok: true })`. Gateway errors in other payload shapes were silently discarded.\n\n## Fix\n\n- Type cast widened to `{ payload?: { result?: unknown; error?: string } }`\n- Error checked first: if `payload.error` is a string, return `{ ok: false, error }`\n- Non-string successful results (number, object) are surfaced as `{ ok: true, result }`\n- Void eval (no error, no result) returns `{ ok: true }`\n- String results are unchanged (existing behavior preserved)\n\nFiles changed:\n- `extensions/canvas/src/tool.ts`: Refactored `case \"eval\"` handler\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Claim proved: Eval errors are surfaced; successful non-string results do not incorrectly return ok:false\n- Commands / artifacts:\n  - `git diff --check` — clean\n  - `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/canvas/src/tool.test.ts` — 12 passed, 1 skipped\n  - Head: `4556618b521`\n",
